<title>USA: Carolina Power Harris 1 trips off line.</title>
<headline>Carolina Power Harris 1 trips off line.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power &amp; Light Co's 880 Megawatt (MW) Harris 1 nuclear power plant tripped off line Thursday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Friday.</p>
<p>The unit tripped off due to &quot;low steam generator water level,&quot; the commission said in its daily status report.</p>
<p>No estimated restart date was given.</p>
<p>The plant is being kept in hot standby, however, indicating a prompt restart is likely.</p>
<p>The Harris nuclear facility is in New Hill, N.C.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1628))</p>
